1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,003
RTLRefine: checked RTL repair with NVIDIA Nemotron on Nebius.
Inspect the failure, source diff and verification evidence in one browser.

2
00:00:08,722 --> 00:00:16,725
Bring a Verilog/SystemVerilog ZIP and your own self-checking benches.
Select file roles in the browser, or include a manifest.

3
00:00:17,095 --> 00:00:26,096
This authored integration example has two files and a 129-bit function.
Its result should be a+b, but the implementation subtracts.

4
00:00:26,124 --> 00:00:30,204
First reproduce the public failure using isolated native tools.
Checking the original makes no model request.

5
00:00:30,204 --> 00:00:34,284
The original fails its public test. No checked project is offered.
The tests remain immutable throughout the repair.

6
00:00:34,284 --> 00:00:40,284
A fresh NVIDIA request through Nebius Token Factory.
The model sees public checks; audit benches stay hidden.

7
00:00:40,284 --> 00:00:49,292
Nemotron changes the subtraction to addition. The exact patch is rebuilt.
Both the public bench and the withheld 40-check audit pass.

8
00:00:49,444 --> 00:00:53,952
Reimport the exported ZIP and run both benches again.
This fresh check makes no model request.

9
00:00:53,952 --> 00:00:58,459
The exported project passes again. Its evidence includes logs and hashes.
Original test files and the project license are preserved.

10
00:00:58,574 --> 00:01:06,578
Now upload an intentionally incomplete developer-written patch.
Changing the project removes the previous successful verdict immediately.

11
00:01:06,578 --> 00:01:12,028
The partial patch passes the public bench and fails the audit.
A checked download is blocked.

12
00:01:12,028 --> 00:01:17,478
Rejected with the failing observations retained.
Acceptance covers only the supplied tests, not unbounded hardware correctness.

13
00:01:18,433 --> 00:01:30,437
Historical examples: the same 118 candidates take 208.08s vs 13.87s.
15.0x screening throughput; matching results, one paired run per profile.

14
00:01:30,437 --> 00:01:38,440
This screening measurement does not apply to uploaded projects.
Their exact files are compiled independently using the supplied benches.

15
00:01:39,044 --> 00:01:47,048
Public source and a Docker test build: github.com/ehdtjq08/RTLRefine
Recorded NVIDIA runs and fresh native checks work without an API key.

